# FH AECB Analyzer -- server environment.
#
# Copy to /etc/aecb-analyzer/aecb.env, fill in, and restrict it:
#   install -d -m 0750 /etc/aecb-analyzer
#   install -m 0600 -o aecb -g aecb deploy/aecb.env.example /etc/aecb-analyzer/aecb.env
# The systemd unit (deploy/aecb-analyzer.service) loads it with EnvironmentFile=.
# Never commit a filled-in copy.

# Bureau-report API service account (IIS Windows authentication, NTLMv2).
# Give the account and its Windows domain separately -- a backslash in this
# file would be read as an escape character.
AECB_API_USERNAME=svc_account
AECB_API_DOMAIN=DOMAIN
AECB_API_PASSWORD=

# Where each successful API response is archived (real bureau data). Must be
# OUTSIDE the application directory; created 0700 with files 0600. Leave
# unset to switch archiving off. Retention is an operations task
# (docs/OPERATIONS.md).
AECB_ARCHIVE_DIR=/var/lib/aecb-analyzer/api_responses

# Rotating application log (aecb.log). Unset: logs go to stderr / journald
# only.
AECB_LOG_DIR=/var/log/aecb-analyzer

# Optional: the request header an SSO reverse proxy sets to the authenticated
# user name, so each audit line records who queried which subject.
#AECB_AUDIT_USER_HEADER=X-Remote-User
